#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0046 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "Authority: ADaM Conformance Rules v5.0 CR46 ('A variable with a suffix of DY has a value of zero'). The suffix names the variable whatever the letter case of the dataset's spelling (column names match case-insensitively, CIT 1; a name tested as a string is folded on the rule side, CIT 3): the lowercase ady = 0 is a DY variable equal to zero -> one violation, reported under the dataset's own spelling ady."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 variable_name=ady
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col studyid type=Char
col usubjid type=Char
col paramcd type=Char
col ady type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | 0
---
